    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Rooney Auctioneers are delighted to present Dursey, North Circular Road, Limerick to the market – an impressive and beautifully maintained 4 bedroom semi-detached residence with large attic room occupying one of Limerick's most prestigious and established residential addresses.\r\n\r\nSituated on the highly sought-after North Circular Road & surrouded by mature trees  this exceptional home enjoys an unrivalled location within walking distance of Limerick City Centre, Villiers School, TUS, the University Hospital Limerick campus, Ted Russell Park and a wealth of local amenities, making it an ideal family home.\r\n\r\nUpon entering, a welcoming entrance hall with attractive light timber flooring provides access to all reception rooms. The ground floor comprises a spacious living room featuring a solid fuel stove and bright south-facing double doors opening onto the rear garden, creating a warm and inviting living space. The light-filled kitchen/ diningroom benefit from a desirable southerly aspect, with large windows, a skylight and a rear door allowing natural light to flood the room throughout the day and providng access to the rear deck area. The kitchen/diningroom also provides direct access to the attached garage, offering excellent storage together with convenient front and rear access. \r\nA ground floor bedroom and guest WC complete the accommodation on this level.\r\n\r\nUpstairs, the first floor comprises three bright generously proportioned bedrooms together with the main family bathroom. A striking wrought iron spiral staircase leads to a versatile second-floor attic room, featuring a south-facing skylight, extensive storage and an attractive space offering endless potential as a home office, studio, hobby room  or additional accommodation, subject to the purchaser's requirements.\r\n\r\nThroughout the property, a wealth of beautiful original features has been carefully preserved, including original timber doors and flooring, adding warmth, character and timeless appeal. These charming period details are complemented by tasteful modern upgrades, including stylish retrofitted radiators throughout the home.\r\n\r\nThe family bathroom features an elegant heritage-style radiator with an integrated heated towel rail, perfectly complementing the property's character.\r\nFurther enhancing the home's efficiency is a modern combi boiler with a two-zone heating system, providing instant hot water and economical day-to-day running costs while eliminating the need for an immersion heater.\r\n\r\nThe property also benefits from the availability of full architectural drawings for further proposed renovations, should the new owner wish to extend or reconfigure the accommodation. This provides excellent potential for future enhancement and added value, subject to the necessary planning permissions.\r\n\r\nDursey presents a rare opportunity to acquire a character-filled family home combining period elegance with modern convenience in one of Limerick's fines residential locations\r\n\r\nEarly viewing is highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall: 3.85m x 2.81m with solid wood origninal flooring and guest WC off. \r\n\r\nGuest WC: 1.42m x 0.89m with Wc, whb.\r\n\r\nKitchen/Diningroom:  3.52m x 2.59m + 4.26m x 3.29m A bright & spacious light-filled  L-shaped kitchen featuring decorative exposed red brick walls and original pine flooring, creating a warm and characterful atmosphere. Large south-facing windows and skylights flood the room with natural light throughout the day, while a door provides direct access to the rear deck and private garden, making it ideal for both everyday living and outdoor entertaining.\r\n\r\nReception Room - 4.39m x 3.50m Rear South facing room with double doors to rear deck and garden and  with a stove.\r\n\r\nDownstairs Bedroom 4 -  3.41m x3.32m Front facing downstairs bedroom\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n1st Floor\r\n\r\nMain Bedroom - 4.41m x 2.86m  A bright and spacious South facing double bedroom.\r\nBedroom 2 - 2.83m x 2.59m  A bright and spacious south-facing rear bedroom.\r\nBedroom 3 - 3.41m x 3.20m  Spacious front-facing double bedroom with built-in wardrobes with vintage pine sliding doors, providing excellent storage\r\n\r\nMain Bathroom - 3.50m x 1.97m Featuring a W.C., wash hand basin, double power shower, and a refurbished original enamel bath, blending timeless character with modern comfort. The room is further enhanced by an elegant heritage-style heated towel rail/radiator.\r\n\r\nAttic Room - 4.23m x 3.20m A spacious and versatile room featuring a large south-facing skylight that fills the space with natural light. Offering ample storage and excellent flexibility, it is ideal for use as a home office, hobby room, playroom or additional living space, subject to the purchaser's needs\r\n\r\nGarage - 7.34m x 3.23m Conveniently accessed from both the front driveway and the rear garden, the garage offers excellent versatility together with a loft area providing valuable additional storage space."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "Additional Features\r\n\r\nBuilt 1930\r\nGas fired central heating (GFCH)\r\nCombi Boiler (2 zone system) \r\nMains water and sewage\r\nDouble-glazed PVC windows\r\nA full set of architectural drawings for the proposed extension and renovation of the property will be included in the sale, providing an excellent opportunity for purchasers to further enhance this superb home, subject to the necessary planning permissions.\r\n\r\nIncluded in Sale\r\n\r\nCarpets, blinds, light fittings & appliances inlcuded\r\n. \r\nOverall Floor Area\r\nApprox. 145.59sq. m. (1566.98sq. ft)\r\n\r\n\r\nThis substantial and versatile home offers exceptionally generous accommodation ideal for growing families, multi-generational living, or those seeking home office space, all complemented by bright reception rooms and practical living areas throughout."
      },
